# ---------------- hook
L("Embarkation day is the most stressful, most expensive and most wasted day of the entire cruise.", ["departing_aerial", "boarding2"], ("title", "17 EMBARKATION DAY MISTAKES"))
L("Not because something goes wrong. Because almost everyone makes the same small mistakes, in the same order, before the ship even leaves the dock.", ["terminal", "travelers_port", "dock_people"])
L("Crew members watch it happen every single week.", ["deck_walk", "maids_bed"])
L("Today I'm walking you through seventeen embarkation day mistakes, split into five phases, from the moment you reach the port to the moment you sail away.", ["cruise_dock", "ship_closeup", "deck_aerial_people"])
L("Avoid them, and your first day feels like a vacation. Ignore them, and you'll spend it standing in lines, overpaying, and waiting for your luggage. Let's fix that.", ["pool_fun", "waiting_floor", "suitcase_zip", "aerial_lux"])
# ---------------- phase 1
L("Phase one. At the port.", ["docked_harbor"], ("phase", 1, "AT THE PORT"))
L("Mistake number one: arriving at the terminal way too early.", ["terminal", "travelers_port"], ("tip", 1, "ARRIVING TOO EARLY"))
L("It feels safe to show up at the crack of dawn. But most cruise lines now give you a check-in window, and if you arrive before it, you simply wait outside, often in the sun, with nowhere to sit.", ["dock_people", "waiting_floor", "boarding1"])
L("Arrive inside your assigned time. Check-in moves faster, and you'll often walk on board within minutes.", ["family_checkin", "aerobridge"])
L("But never cut it close either. Boarding usually closes an hour or more before departure, and the ship will not wait for you.", ["leaving_sunset", "prima_departing"])
L("Mistake number two: packing everything you need in your checked luggage.", ["suitcase_zip", "luggage_close"], ("tip", 2, "EVERYTHING IN CHECKED BAGS"))
L("When you hand your bags to the porters, they disappear for hours. On a big ship, they may not reach your cabin until the evening.", ["family_trunk", "xray", "corridor"])
L("So pack a small carry-on as if it's your first day. Documents, medication, phone charger, sunscreen, a swimsuit, and a change of clothes for dinner.", ["luggage_fold", "passport_check"])
L("Then you can hit the pool at noon, while everyone else is still waiting for their suitcase.", ["pool_father", "pool_selfie"])
L("Pro tip: put a tag with your name and cabin number on your carry-on too. If you leave it somewhere on deck, the crew can bring it straight back.", ["luggage_close", "deck_walk"])
L("Mistake number three: not having your documents ready in your hand.", ["passport_stamps", "passport_check"], ("tip", 3, "DOCUMENTS NOT READY"))
L("Passport or whatever ID your cruise line requires, boarding pass, luggage tags, and the cruise app already set up on your phone.", ["passport_check", "phone_typing"])
L("On a round trip cruise from the United States, a birth certificate and photo ID are often accepted. But a passport protects you if you ever need to fly home from a foreign port.", ["passport_stamps", "aerobridge"])
L("Digging through a backpack at the check-in desk is how a ten minute process turns into forty.", ["hotel_reception", "waiting_floor"])
# ---------------- phase 2
L("Phase two. The first hour on board.", ["carnival_deck"], ("phase", 2, "THE FIRST HOUR ON BOARD"))
L("Mistake number four: going straight to the buffet.", ["buffet", "restaurant_tables"], ("tip", 4, "THE BUFFET RUSH"))
L("It's the first place everyone goes, so for the first few hours it becomes the most crowded room on the ship.", ["restaurant_tables", "buffet"])
L("On many ships, the main dining room or a smaller cafe is also open for lunch on embarkation day, with table service and half the noise. Check the app to see what's open.", ["waiter_dish", "restaurant_min", "phone_scroll"])
L("And if you do go to the buffet, walk the whole thing once before you pick up a plate. The best stations are often at the far end, where the line is shortest.", ["buffet", "hotel_breakfast"])
L("Mistake number five: putting off the safety drill.", ["lifeboats", "ship_board"], ("tip", 5, "PUTTING OFF THE DRILL"))
L("Every passenger has to complete the muster drill, and most cruise lines require it before the ship sails. It's an international safety rule.", ["lifeboats", "deck_sea"])
L("Many lines now use a quick digital version. You watch a short safety video in the app, then check in at your assigned muster station.", ["phone_typing", "deck_view"])
L("Do it early. Wait too long, and you'll get calls to your cabin or hear your name over the speakers. And knowing where your station is could one day really matter.", ["corridor", "lifeboats"])
L("Pro tip: walk the route from your cabin to your muster station once. In an emergency, you use the stairs, not the elevators.", ["corridor", "ship_board"])
L("Mistake number six: not booking dinners, shows and the spa on day one.", ["stage_light", "spa_massage"], ("tip", 6, "NOT BOOKING ON DAY ONE"))
L("Specialty restaurants, popular shows and spa appointments fill up fast.", ["waiter_wine", "theater_actors", "spa_face"])
L("Some lines even offer embarkation day discounts on specialty dining or spa treatments, because they want to fill those seats early.", ["toast_wine", "spa_massage"])
L("Ten minutes in the app on day one can save you money and a lot of disappointment later.", ["phone_happy", "outdoor_dining"])
L("Mistake number seven: leaving your phone on cellular data.", ["phone_sunset", "phone_bed"], ("tip", 7, "CELLULAR DATA AT SEA"))
L("Once the ship leaves port, your phone may connect to a maritime network at sea. And those roaming rates can be shockingly expensive.", ["ocean_cruise", "texting_night"])
L("Switch to airplane mode before you sail, turn Wi-Fi back on, and use the ship's internet package if you need to stay connected.", ["phone_typing", "sea_from_ship"])
L("While you're at it, pause automatic app updates and photo backups. On a slow ship connection, they can quietly eat your whole internet allowance.", ["phone_bed", "window_sea"])
L("Mistake number eight: not exploring the ship while it's quiet.", ["deck_walk", "elevators"], ("tip", 8, "NOT EXPLORING EARLY"))
L("The first few hours are the only time you'll see the pool deck, the theater and the quiet corners without the crowds.", ["carnival_deck", "stage_light", "deck_ocean"])
L("Walk the ship from top to bottom. Find the elevators nearest your cabin, the guest services desk, and the best spot to watch the sail away.", ["elevators", "corridor", "deck_view"])
# ---------------- phase 3
L("Phase three. The money traps.", ["money_count"], ("phase", 3, "THE MONEY TRAPS"))
L("Mistake number nine: buying a drink package without reading the rules.", ["cocktail_bar", "bar_busy"], ("tip", 9, "DRINK PACKAGE RULES"))
L("On some cruise lines, if one adult in the cabin buys an alcohol package, every adult in that cabin has to buy it too.", ["cocktails", "woman_cocktail"])
L("And a package usually only pays off if you drink a lot, every single day. Do the math before you tap buy.", ["bartender", "card_phone"])
L("Look at the drink prices on the bar menu, multiply by what you really drink in a day, and compare that with the package price, including the service charge.", ["cocktail_bar", "credit_laptop"])
L("Mistake number ten: forgetting about automatic gratuities.", ["money_count", "coins"], ("tip", 10, "AUTOMATIC GRATUITIES"))
L("Most lines add a daily service charge to your onboard account, per person, per day.", ["card_terminal", "maid_bed2"])
L("On a seven day cruise for a family of four, that can add up to hundreds of dollars you didn't plan for. Budget for it from day one.", ["family_arriving", "wallet_empty"])
L("On many lines you can prepay gratuities before the cruise, so they don't surprise you at the end. Just remember that the crew really depends on them.", ["card_phone", "towels_bed"])
L("Mistake number eleven: never checking your onboard account.", ["credit_laptop", "card_phone"], ("tip", 11, "NOT CHECKING YOUR ACCOUNT"))
L("Everything on board is charged to your cruise card. Drinks, photos, spa treatments, specialty coffee.", ["card_pos", "bar_busy", "spa_face"])
L("Check your account in the app every day or two, so mistakes or surprise charges get fixed while you're still on the ship, not after you get home.", ["phone_scroll", "card_phone"])
L("Mistake number twelve: falling for the first day sales pitch.", ["card_pos", "toast"], ("tip", 12, "FIRST DAY SALES PITCH"))
L("Art auctions, photo packages, jewelry deals and future cruise offers all compete for your attention on day one.", ["stage_light", "credit_laptop"])
L("Some of them are genuinely good value. But don't buy anything in the excitement of the first afternoon. Compare first, and decide later in the week.", ["phone_happy", "deck_ocean"])
# ---------------- phase 4
L("Phase four. Your cabin.", ["porthole"], ("phase", 4, "YOUR CABIN"))
L("Mistake number thirteen: unpacking before you check the cabin.", ["hotel_pan", "luggage_close"], ("tip", 13, "UNPACKING BEFORE CHECKING"))
L("Before anything goes into a drawer, take a quick look around.", ["hotel_small", "hotel_pan2"])
L("Check the air conditioning, the toilet, the shower, the safe and the balcony door. If something is broken, report it right away, while there's still time to fix it or move you.", ["ac", "shower", "balcony_sunset"])
L("Pro tip: take a quick video of the cabin as you found it. If there's any damage, you'll have proof that it was already there.", ["phone_typing", "hotel_pan2"])
L("Mistake number fourteen: living out of your suitcase.", ["suitcase_zip", "hotel_modern"], ("tip", 14, "LIVING OUT OF YOUR SUITCASE"))
L("Cruise cabins are small, but they hide more storage than most people expect. There's often space under the bed and in cupboards you'll only find if you look.", ["hotel_white", "luggage_fold"])
L("Unpack completely, slide the empty suitcase under the bed, and the cabin suddenly feels twice as big.", ["hotel_terrace", "girl_bed"])
L("Mistake number fifteen: not talking to your cabin steward.", ["maids_bed", "towels_bed"], ("tip", 15, "IGNORING YOUR STEWARD"))
L("Your steward is the person who can make your whole week easier. Introduce yourself, learn their name, and ask for what you need.", ["maid_bed2", "fix_bed"])
L("Extra pillows, an ice bucket, a different bed setup. Asking on day one is much easier than on day four.", ["towels_rack", "family_bathrobes"])
L("And if you like to tip in cash, a small thank you early in the week is often remembered for the rest of the trip.", ["money_count", "maids_bed"])
# ---------------- phase 5
L("Phase five. Before you sail away.", ["leaving_sunset"], ("phase", 5, "BEFORE YOU SAIL AWAY"))
L("Mistake number sixteen: missing the sail away.", ["departing_aerial", "ship_pov"], ("tip", 16, "MISSING THE SAIL AWAY"))
L("Leaving port is one of the most beautiful moments of the whole trip, and many people miss it because they're unpacking or taking a nap.", ["prima_departing", "tired_man"])
L("Head up to an open deck, grab a drink, and watch the coastline slide away. You only get this moment once per cruise.", ["pink_sky_deck", "woman_cocktail", "sunset_ship"])
L("Pro tip: the party is usually at the pool, but the calmest view is often at the back of the ship, where you can watch the wake and the port shrink behind you.", ["waves_ship", "ocean_aerial"])
L("And mistake number seventeen: trying to do everything on the first night.", ["night_aerial", "bar_busy"], ("tip", 17, "DOING EVERYTHING NIGHT ONE"))
L("It's tempting to stay out until two in the morning. But day two often starts with an early port, an excursion, or a sea day you'll want to enjoy.", ["night_sea", "alarm", "drone_pr"])
L("Get some sleep. The best cruisers pace themselves, and they feel great on day seven, not just on day one.", ["lights_off", "wake_up"])
L("Before bed, check tomorrow's schedule in the app, so you know what time the ship arrives and what's happening on board.", ["phone_bed", "harbor_night"])
# ---------------- outro
L("So here's the short version. Arrive on time, pack a smart carry-on, keep your documents in hand, skip the buffet rush, finish your safety drill early, book what matters, turn off cellular data, and walk the ship.", ["aerial_sea", "ship_sunset_lux", "deck_aerial_people"], ("recap", 1))
L("Read the drink rules, budget for gratuities, check your account, don't rush big purchases, inspect and unpack your cabin, say hello to your steward, enjoy the sail away, and get some sleep.", ["ship_istanbul", "balcony_sunset", "harbor_night"], ("recap", 2))
